00:37:27,481 --> 00:37:29,080
We have to monitor it constantly.

450
00:37:32,520 --> 00:37:36,480
Precision and attention to detail are equally vital during the Intaglio printing.

451
00:37:37,380 --> 00:37:39,680
An old process with a new look.

452
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:43,540
The concept of Intaglio printing remains the same.

453
00:37:43,660 --> 00:37:51,000
It's just that we take advantage of modern technology to deliver that concept in a quicker, faster, more economical way.

454
00:37:52,040 --> 00:37:57,460
The Intaglio presses can print as many as 10,000 of the 32 note sheets every hour.

455
00:37:57,980 --> 00:38:00,060
But only one side at a time.

456
00:38:00,061 --> 00:38:03,060
They turn out the reverse sides first.

457
00:38:03,061 --> 00:38:07,060
This is the sheet that has been removed from the back intaglio press,

458
00:38:07,061 --> 00:38:12,060
and the press will examine the sheet for various flaws that occur during the process.

459
00:38:12,061 --> 00:38:19,060
They'll examine all sides, even both the side that's unprinted and also the printed side.

460
00:38:19,061 --> 00:38:23,060
The printed sheets are set aside to air dry for three days.

461
00:38:23,061 --> 00:38:26,060
Then the front sides are printed.

462
00:38:26,061 --> 00:38:33,060
After another three days of drying, the paper is cut in half into 16-note sheets.

463
00:38:33,061 --> 00:38:40,060
Then, during a process called overprinting, a letterpress adds three crucial final touches.

464
00:38:40,061 --> 00:38:45,060
These are the sheets that are coming out of the delivery of the currency overprinting machine.

465
00:38:45,061 --> 00:38:51,060
They now have the serial numbers on them, the unique Federal Reserve seal, and also the Treasury seal.

466
00:38:51,061 --> 00:38:59,820
treasury seal next the now fully printed sheets are cut into two note units and

467
00:38:59,821 --> 00:39:06,240
then into single bills all that's left is to band a hundred notes together at a

468
00:39:06,241 --> 00:39:12,180
time have an examiner give them a quick once-over and bundle them together for

469
00:39:12,181 --> 00:39:19,080
shipment to the Fed as the Bureau of Engraving and Printing continues to

470
00:39:19,081 --> 00:39:26,080
write the book on creating money, another facility has become just as adept at destroying it.

471
00:39:31,440 --> 00:39:36,420
The bill with the highest denomination ever produced by the Bureau of Engraving and Printing

472
00:39:36,421 --> 00:39:40,159
was the $100,000 gold certificate, series 1934.

473
00:39:40,160 --> 00:39:43,420
It was used only for transactions between

474
00:39:43,421 --> 00:39:45,200
between federal reserve banks.

475
00:39:46,240 --> 00:39:48,500
Money will return on Modern Marvels.

476
00:39:49,880 --> 00:39:53,120
We now return to money on Modern Marvels.

477
00:39:59,580 --> 00:40:02,220
If you like the new look of American currency

478
00:40:02,221 --> 00:40:03,580
over the past several years,

479
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:05,420
don't get too used to it.

480
00:40:06,340 --> 00:40:08,320
To stay a step ahead of the counterfeiters,

481
00:40:09,080 --> 00:40:10,460
government officials have decided

482
00:40:10,461 --> 00:40:12,220
that the Bureau of Engraving and Printing

483
00:40:12,221 --> 00:40:15,960
will produce a redesigned banknote every seven to ten years.

484
00:40:18,080 --> 00:40:21,180
But no matter how often and how much we change our money,

485
00:40:21,840 --> 00:40:23,720
it'll never be safe from the copycats.

486
00:40:25,080 --> 00:40:28,100
There is no such thing as a counterfeit-proof note.

487
00:40:28,620 --> 00:40:33,160
The reality is, with enough time, resources, effort,

488
00:40:33,520 --> 00:40:37,180
you can duplicate or simulate any document.

489
00:40:37,181 --> 00:40:43,680
The technology available through consumer products, through desktop printers, through software,

490
00:40:44,320 --> 00:40:52,020
has brought the counterfeiter toolkit to a level of sophistication that just didn't exist 15 years ago.

491
00:40:52,540 --> 00:40:54,140
All you need is a finger.

492
00:40:54,600 --> 00:41:00,700
One finger, you push a button on a color copier, and you've got a simulated counterfeit note.

493
00:41:00,701 --> 00:41:08,640
Since 1865, the United States Secret Service has sought out counterfeit cash and arrested offenders.

494
00:41:10,380 --> 00:41:13,880
In recent years, its agents have confronted a bold new threat.

495
00:41:14,980 --> 00:41:20,140
Counterfeit hundred-dollar bills of such high quality that they're called supernotes.

496
00:41:22,160 --> 00:41:25,840
Investigators determined that the supernotes are printed on cotton fiber paper,

497
00:41:26,560 --> 00:41:30,100
using the same kind of intaglio presses operating at the BEP.

498
00:41:30,700 --> 00:41:36,520
The bills were finally traced to a government-financed facility in North Korea.

499
00:41:37,940 --> 00:41:43,600
Supernotes elevated the level of counterfeiting beyond the reach of anything

500
00:41:43,601 --> 00:41:48,880
those of us in the business of anti-counterfeit technology thought we'd have to confront,

501
00:41:49,780 --> 00:41:51,600
state-sponsored counterfeiting.

502
00:41:52,520 --> 00:41:57,080
If a counterfeiter has state resources, that's difficult.

503
00:41:57,081 --> 00:42:05,440
There isn't anything that we believe we can do from a design perspective to address state resources.

504
00:42:06,820 --> 00:42:13,120
The American government hopes to shut down the North Korean operation through diplomacy and international law enforcement.

505
00:42:14,660 --> 00:42:18,740
Most Americans could never tell the difference between a supernote and the real thing.

506
00:42:19,520 --> 00:42:24,100
But the fakes are spotted with relative ease at the 12 branches of the Federal Reserve Bank.

507
00:42:24,101 --> 00:42:29,620
Authentic currency contains covert features that Super Notes lack

508
00:42:29,621 --> 00:42:34,120
And the Fed's high-speed processing equipment automatically detects the difference

509
00:42:34,121 --> 00:42:42,240
It's all part of the Federal Reserve's duty to manage the flood of newly printed and circulating currency shipped to its branches

510
00:42:42,241 --> 00:42:48,060
The New York branch processes over 13 million notes every day

511
00:42:51,060 --> 00:42:53,700
All the while, its shredders do the dirty work

512
00:42:53,701 --> 00:42:56,460
destroying 4 million unfit bills daily.

513
00:42:57,860 --> 00:43:00,420
The shreds hurtle to a disposal area,

514
00:43:00,820 --> 00:43:02,660
where they're compressed into small blocks.

515
00:43:04,780 --> 00:43:08,660
Some experts believe we'll someday be able to trash all our currency,

516
00:43:09,160 --> 00:43:12,940
as electronic alternatives offer the promise of a cashless society.

517
00:43:14,540 --> 00:43:19,140
Today you see much more readily the acceptance of credit cards and debit cards

518
00:43:19,141 --> 00:43:20,440
for low-value transactions.

519
00:43:20,441 --> 00:43:27,120
Tollboots, laundromats, most retail outlets now are eager for you to use your credit card

520
00:43:27,121 --> 00:43:28,880
or debit card in lieu of cash.

521
00:43:28,881 --> 00:43:37,660
And if you look at transactions increasingly, there are points where paper money is actually

522
00:43:37,661 --> 00:43:43,400
a burden, but there are transactions that require anonymity.

523
00:43:43,401 --> 00:43:49,720
And as long as there's a need for anonymity, there will be a need for bank notes.

524
00:43:49,721 --> 00:43:54,780
If currency and coins stand the test of time, it won't be just because we want to avoid

525
00:43:54,781 --> 00:43:57,480
leaving an electronic signature.

526
00:43:57,481 --> 00:44:03,320
Our money expresses our national identity and our cultural character.

527
00:44:03,321 --> 00:44:07,320
Coins will always be around in large measure because they represent something very important

528
00:44:07,321 --> 00:44:09,540
about a country.

529
00:44:09,541 --> 00:44:14,640
The important values of our nation, in God we trust, unity,

